==English==

===Interjection===
'''my bad'''

===Etymology===
# {{colloquial}} {{idiom|English}} my fault.
Seems to have originated from a phase by Manute Bol, A player of Sudanese origin for Golden State Warriors in Bay area. Other players picked it up and started using it.

===Phrase===
#: ''Yes, I realize the humvee isn't supposed to be parked in the heirloom flowerbed.  My bad.''

